  "notes": "USAGE: {針|はり} refers to needles in general and clock hands. In medical contexts, it often means acupuncture.\n\nTYPES OF NEEDLES:\n・{縫|ぬ}い{針|ばり} (sewing needle)\n・{編|あ}み{針|ばり} (knitting needle)\n・{注射|ちゅうしゃ}{針|ばり} (injection needle)\n・{釣|つ}り{針|ばり} (fishhook)\n\nCLOCK-RELATED:\n・{長|なが}い{針|はり} (minute hand)\n・{短|みじか}い{針|はり} (hour hand)\n・{秒|びょう}{針|しん} (second hand)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n・{針|はり}の{穴|あな}を{通|とお}すよう (like threading a needle - very difficult)\n・{針小棒大|しんしょうぼうだい} (making a mountain out of a molehill)",
